executionContract.intendedBehavior:
runCheckSession validates its inputs, including isOwnedInstanceName(name). It then opens its stream only through openGuestStream({name, mode: 'check', provider}): the pinned ssh client with exactly sshStreamArgv for the fresh info address. Outcomes:
- a transport refusal is 'infra-failure' with nothing spawned;
- ssh's own exit 255 is 'infra-failure' with exitCode null, before or after hello;
- the supervisor's 79, 80, 81 and 82 keep their outcomes;
- the budget still starts at spawn, so a dead stdin or a stdout stall ends in 'timeout';
- an abort during the info read ends in 'infra-failure' without writing the frame.
certify's watchedSession forwards the whole context provider (run, ssh, keyDir) with its own watched spawn.
